Fillets: a blend rolling on an edge (surface/restriction walking) stopped
where a step was too large (mitcad#121).

BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder::InternalPerform: a section whose contacts lie
outside their domains and cannot be reframed on an arc (on the surface, on
the restriction, or where the ball leaves the restriction) ended the walk
at once (Blend_SamePoints). A step that is too large lands such sections:
on a long rounding the guide's maximal step reaches the other branch of
the solution (a ball on the far side of the restriction), whose contact
lies outside the face. As BRepBlend_Walking does for blends between two
faces, the step is now halved (Blend_StepTooLarge) while it is larger than
twice the guide's tolerance; only then does the walk stop there.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder.cxx
